Package: measuredES
Type: Package
Title: Measurement-Corrected Effect Sizes for the Behavioral Sciences
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Fazilet Gül", family = "İnce Aracı",
           email = "gulincegazi@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5620-6911")),
    person(given = "Eren Halil", family = "Özberk",
           role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2136-3081")))
Description: Computes effect sizes corrected for attenuation due to
    measurement unreliability: Cohen's d and Hedges' g for two-group
    comparisons, and Pearson r for bivariate correlations. Implements the
    classical disattenuation formula of Spearman (1904)
    <doi:10.2307/1412159>, the Hunter-Schmidt psychometric meta-analysis
    framework, and analytical and bootstrap confidence intervals following
    Charles (2005) <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.10.2.206> and Bonett (2008)
    <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.13.2.99>. Fisher-z intervals are provided for
    corrected correlations. Produces APA-7 style reports and
    'metafor'-compatible meta-analytic data structures.
